*.log

# Claude Code local settings (per-machine)
.claude/settings.local.json

# MS Office lock/owner files
~$*

# Client bank statements - this repo is PUBLIC. These PDFs carry the station's
# account numbers, IFSC codes, customer name and address. Kept local on purpose
# (2026-09-13); delete these two lines only with the owner's say-so.
docs/01-BRD-Requirement-Gathering/ocr-samples/SVR_DSR_13SEP26/Account_Statement_Last_10_transactions-3.pdf
docs/01-BRD-Requirement-Gathering/ocr-samples/SVR_DSR_13SEP26/AccountStatement-4.pdf
docs/01-BRD-Requirement-Gathering/ocr-samples/SEP14/AccountStatement-5.pdf

# SEP16 bank statements - confidential, uploaded for read-only review only
# (client, 2026-09-16). This repo is PUBLIC.
docs/01-BRD-Requirement-Gathering/ocr-samples/SEP16/Account Statement - SVR INDIANOIL SERVICE STATION.pdf
docs/01-BRD-Requirement-Gathering/ocr-samples/SEP16/AccountStatement.pdf
docs/01-BRD-Requirement-Gathering/ocr-samples/SEP16/Account_Statement_Last_10_transactions.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STANDING RULE, set by the owner 2026-09-24:
#   "Never push Bank statements or IFSC codes or any financial data."
#   "DO NOT PUSH ANY EXCEL SHEETS OR FINANCIAL DATA."
#
# This repo is PUBLIC. Everything below stays on the station PC. Do not remove
# any of these lines, or narrow them, without the owner saying so in as many
# words. Blanket patterns on purpose: the per-file list above this block only
# caught the statements someone happened to notice, and a new file with a new
# name would have gone straight up.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Every spreadsheet under docs/ - the DSR and Trial Balance workbooks carry the
# station's daily cash, bank balances, credits and profit.
docs/**/*.xlsx
docs/**/*.xlsm
docs/**/*.xls
docs/**/*.csv

# Any bank or dealer account statement, whatever it is called or where it sits.
**/[Aa]ccount[ _-]*[Ss]tatement*
**/[Ss]tatement*[Oo]f*[Aa]ccount*
**/AccountStatement*

# The dated testing uploads: filled forms, exports and statements. Working
# material for the testing rounds, not repository content.
#
# Was one explicit folder per date (SEP14, SEP15, SEP16, SEP24...) - a list
# that has to be remembered and extended by hand every single day the work
# moves forward, and "SVR Sales Report-*.pdf" under SEP28 slipped straight
# through it undetected (2026-09-28) exactly like the earlier zip and
# no-separator filename gaps. A real day's folder is always THREE-LETTER-
# MONTH + DIGITS (SEP28, OCT05, ...) - catch the whole shape once, generically,
# instead of one more name to add by hand next time the date rolls over.
docs/01-BRD-Requirement-Gathering/ocr-samples/[A-Z][A-Z][A-Z][0-9]*/
docs/01-BRD-Requirement-Gathering/ocr-samples/Testing_Results_Sep15/
docs/01-BRD-Requirement-Gathering/ocr-samples/NEW_PRINT_FORMS/
docs/01-BRD-Requirement-Gathering/ocr-samples/EMPTY_PRINTING_FORMS/

# Uploaded archives of the station's own paperwork (a .zip hides its contents
# from every pattern above - trailbalance24september2026.zip arrived while this
# block was being written and would otherwise have been the one thing pushed).
#
# [_ ]* here means "one separator char, then anything" in glob syntax, NOT
# "zero or more separators" (that's regex thinking, not glob) - so
# "trailbalance27september2026.zip" (no separator at all) slipped straight
# through this rule undetected until caught 2026-09-27. Plain `*` (zero or
# more of ANY character) is what actually covers the no-separator case.
docs/01-BRD-Requirement-Gathering/ocr-samples/**/*.zip
docs/**/[Tt]rail*balance*
docs/**/[Tt]rial*balance*
